model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Protocol 38 and framework basalt.13 add isolated app cloud-drive callbacks without changing frozen protocols. Agent mutations retain native approval and active workflow checks. Batches are bounded to one hundred edits. Reads pin a Git revision; conflicts preserve writer branches and accepted history never expires. record storage is canonical while session indexes and caches are disposable. Admission reports the exact exhausted quota through the installed framework. The first import uses a sealed file manifest and separate counted record-storage operation allowance; ordinary saves cannot borrow it. Desktop mirrors attachment bytes while mobile downloads on open or pin, and eviction only removes verified local copies. Connect grants the selected app protocol through a person-scoped revocable connection. Large Markdown remains readable and searchable through bounded byte continuations, and all Markdown stays offline on mobile. Device direct calls bind the app identity so renames cannot redirect or break them. Authoring files remain byte-exact compressed build data, decoded only when requested. Feature deployment requires a separately provisioned retained bucket and compatible drive migration observed on the live environment before bindings become available."
    }
  }
}
